dle 5 marks up a branch node, since a wrapper span around the text would break the xpath's exact match on `span` text.\n\nI'm wondering whether the text span sits deeper than a direct child of the `p`, which would break the current lookup. A more robust match would search for the span at any depth inside the branch paragraph, as long as it still targets the same node.\n\nI'm considering a broader xpath for the text node that matches the span at any depth inside the branch paragraph, and maybe accepting aria-expanded on either the p or the li, so the lookup works whichever structure the new UI uses.\n\nI'm going to loosen the text-node lookup so the span can sit at any depth under the branch paragraph, not only as a direct child. That covers the case where the new UI wraps the label in an extra element, while the paragraph and list structure stay as they are.\n\nI'm considering switching the text lookup from direct `span` and `a` children to a descendant match, since the label may be nested one level deeper in the new UI. I'd apply that to both the top-level and nested xpath alternatives in the same step.\n\nI'm making the xpath for the text node match the span or link at any depth under the branch paragraph, not just as a direct child. The collapsed-state and branch conditions and the exact text match stay the same, so it still targets the same node.\n\n"}}
